.git
# CI lives outside the image. Stage one is `COPY . .`, so without these the workflows and the
# smoke gate would land in the build context: they would be baked into the frontend stage, and
# — worse — editing a workflow or ci/smoke.py would invalidate that COPY layer and force a full
# `npm ci` + `vite build` rebuild for a change no build input depends on.
# `.github/` is kept alongside `.gitea/` although it is empty today: a mirror or a lint workflow
# reappearing there should not quietly become a build input again.
.github/
.gitea/
ci/
.claude/
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
dist/
dist-ssr/
release/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
data/
server/data/
tests/
server/tests/
pytest.ini
*.md
.DS_Store
*.local
